    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_f3409925",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: we_sware_we_d_never_forget_911; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts the burning Twin Towers of the World Trade Center during the 9/11 attacks, overlaid with the text 'we swore we'd never forget' and '911'. The overall intent is to evoke strong emotional reactions by visually associating the traumatic event with a promise of remembrance. While not explicitly targeting any specific group with hate or abuse, the meme's harmful nature stems from its potential to trigger intense grief, trauma, and distress in viewers who experienced or were affected by the event. It may also be used in contexts that trivialize or exploit the tragedy for shock value or political commentary, which can be deeply offensive and potentially harmful to survivors, families of victims, and the broader public. The juxtaposition of the image with the text serves to reinforce the gravity of the event and the enduring emotional weight it carries, but its use in certain contexts can be seen as insensitive or exploitative.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_515326ab"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
