      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "911_Attacks",
      "label": "September 11, 2001 Attacks",
      "description": "The terrorist attacks on the World Trade Center in New York City, which resulted in the destruction of the Twin Towers and the loss of nearly 3,000 lives. This event is globally recognized as one of the most significant and traumatic in modern history, and its imagery is deeply associated with national grief and remembrance.",
